narrative:
I am XXXX XXXX and I am submitting this complaint myself and there is no third party involved. 

I XXXX XXXX consumer, natural person an Original Creditor of an open-end credit plan was denied my right of credit by Capital One was notified of the transgression of my rights specifically 15 usc 1601 The Truth In Lending Act by Capital One On XX/XX/XXXX via US mail according to 15 usc 1602 definitions of the Truth In Lending Act I as a natural person possessing an open end credit plan was harmed by Capital One adverse action taken against me denying my rights. And in Capital Ones Response to my consumer credit application Capital One also discriminated and discouraged me an applicant from applying for an extension of credit by noting in there letter that they are taking adverse action on the grounds of a consumer report that was provided to them by a consumer reporting agency called Early Warning Services which is a direct violation of 15 usc 1681m ( C ) ( i ) ( I ), ( ii ) which states that grounds for an adverse action can not include or be on the grounds of information in a consumer report, and can not be based off of information solely as to transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person furnishing the information. 

Capital one is now civilly liable for discrimination and discouraging me the consumer pursuant to 15 usc 1691e ( a ), ( b ) ; and Capital one is criminally liable pursuant to 15 usc 1611 for failure to disclose the cost of consumer credit pursuant to 15 usc 1611 and owes {$5000.00}
